# Examples that are known to fail the audit.
#
# The audit runs every example in examples/pyash through the real runner and
# gates on regressions: a failure that is listed here keeps being reported but
# does not fail the run, and any failure that is not listed fails the run.
#
# Remove an entry once its example passes; the audit reports the ones that
# have been fixed so the list stays honest.
#
# The entries below share one root cause each, and both are defects in the
# repository rather than in the examples. They are tracked in
# documentation/remediation-plan.md under "Phase 2 findings that need an owner
# decision".
#
# The agent session examples collide on one turn id: a turn id is derived from
# the exchange sentence id, and the exchange sentence id is the sentence index
# in the run, so two runs reach the same id and the shared session ledger
# reports conflicting evidence for it.
#
#   agent-session.pya
#   agent-session-fromtext-name.pya
#   coding-loop-guarantee.pya
#
# The session examples need an interactive terminal: the audit runs examples
# without a stdin, and the session verb waits for input that never arrives
# instead of saying that it cannot run.
#
#   agent-session-loop.pya
#   mind-session.pya
#
# su name known_failures ob ve text ya
su name known_failures ob text "agent-session.pya" ya
su name known_failures ob text "agent-session-fromtext-name.pya" ya
su name known_failures ob text "agent-session-loop.pya" ya
su name known_failures ob text "mind-session.pya" ya
su name known_failures ob text "coding-loop-guarantee.pya" ya
prah
